# Manifest of the gd test suites scripts/run-gd-tests.sh MUST find under
# drive/tests/gd/. Line format (v2, shared with pcb/ and cad/):
#
#     <filename> [assertions=N] [real-worker]
#
# - <filename>: exactly as it appears on disk. A suite going missing
#   (deleted, renamed, moved off the glob) or appearing unregistered is a
#   loud, named pre-flight failure in both directions.
# - assertions=N: the suite must report exactly N total assertions
#   (passed+failed), so `check(true); quit(0)` planted above the real
#   assertions FAILS instead of passing a bare floor. Re-pin honestly when a
#   suite legitimately grows or shrinks.
# - real-worker: refused here — the attribute is a claim about a live worker
#   and drive ships no scripts/probe-worker-methods.py to back it.

# The real broker + real drive backend weigh a minerva_drive_list reply past
# the host's 64 KiB control cap and assert the panel drew a row for every
# project the worker sent. Pinned for a host where the drive plugin is
# already installed and built: an install (or its cargo_build pipeline) adds
# its own setup assertions, and the suite skips its live sections outright
# when drive-plugin is not built or when DRIVE_FOLDER does not reach the
# subprocess.
# 14 assertions = 4 setup (channel declared, start, panel, bulk route) + 2
# the backend answered at all and is working in the scratch folder + 4 the
# weighed reply + 3 the drawn rows + 1 teardown.
test_bulk_reply_seam.gd assertions=14
